# Vitamin Helix — Projects/Detail/Briefing Redesign: Architecture Decisions

**Status:** Living document. Captures decisions for work still ahead. The Projects *list* page is live — its architecture/conventions/state live in `Projects.md`, not here. This doc carries the still-ahead work: the **Detail + Briefing overlay** (the big rework), plus the cross-cutting status/role/data-model changes it introduces.

**Last updated:** 30 Jul 2026 — **The Detail + Briefing redesign is now locked as an OVERLAY, not a new page** (the "new idea" the 28 Jul note flagged). This supersedes every 17 Jul 2026 "second-rail / separate-page / two-parallel-submission-cards" wireframe section — those have been replaced below by the locked overlay model. The step-by-step build plan lives in a separate companion doc, **`Projects Rework Workflow.md`**.

---

## Ground rules for this whole initiative

1. **Scope of "rewrite from scratch":** templates, CSS, JS, and route *rendering* logic for the Projects page(s), Detail page, and Briefing/Create page. NOT the DB schema wholesale (migrations are additive, no data loss on deploy) and NOT most of the proven backend business logic (query functions, the status-log funnel, notification triggers, achievement hooks) — that gets reused/refactored-in-place, not re-derived from memory, unless a specific piece is confirmed broken below.
2. **Benchmark:** the Dashboard is the visual and code-quality bar. It is NOT being redesigned (one small additive exception: Escalation History).
3. **Sequencing:** Projects list page — done (see `Projects.md`). Detail + Briefing overlay — next, as ONE combined rework (Briefing is folded in as the overlay's Create mode; see below). Execution order is milestone-by-milestone per `Projects Rework Workflow.md`.
4. **Branch:** work happens on `dev`. `main` stays clean/deployable.
5. **Working mode:** Ezekiel writes the code himself, rebuilding manual-coding muscle memory. Claude/Sonnet gives code + explanation **one chunk at a time with line references**, never applies it directly, unless Ezekiel grants a one-time exception. Every chunk is verified working before the next.
6. **Future-migration principle (17 Jul 2026):** eventual move to Flutter once HR/production/accounting modules exist. Write clean, modular code with business logic decoupled from templates/routes so migration is easier — but do NOT build a separate JSON API layer yet (deferred until the app's shape stabilizes). The overlay fetches HTML fragments on demand (same as the Projects-page row-expansion), not a JSON API.
7. **Client-side performance principle (21 Jul 2026)** — render-on-demand, not render-everything-and-hide. See below. The overlay reinforces this: content is injected on open and torn down on close.

---

## Client-Side Performance (locked 21 Jul 2026)

Server response time is not the bottleneck anywhere in this app; client-side rendering/DOM cost is. Root causes found in the Dashboard (for reference): every card's full body renders into the DOM for every tab regardless of active state; `initCards()` forces a synchronous `scrollHeight` layout read in a loop on load; `dashboard.js` is one 162KB file serving every role; avatars aren't lazy-loaded.

**Principle for the new work, going forward:**
- **Don't pre-render collapsed/inactive states.** The overlay's rail sub-sections and phase tabs build/inject their markup when actually shown (fetch-on-click, or clone from a `<template>`), not at first paint.
- **Never force a layout read (`scrollHeight`/`offsetHeight`/`getBoundingClientRect`) inside a loop right after a DOM write.** Measure in one pass, write in another.
- **Event delegation, not one listener per row** (90+ deliverables in C&CM). One listener on a shared container, read `event.target.closest(...)` — same pattern proven on the Projects page.
- **JS split per surface** so a given view only loads the JS it needs.
- **Debounce live-filter/search inputs.**
- **Lazy-load avatar images** (`loading="lazy"`).

**Dashboard optimization pass — explicitly deferred, not part of this scope.**

---

## New scope items agreed during architecture alignment

- **Soft-delete + admin archive** (see Cancel/Archive in the overlay model below — cancel is the primary path; hard-delete is the rare admin permanent removal).
- **Escalation History on the dashboard.** `DecisionFlag`/`DecisionFlagMessage` is the real, live "Decisions Needed" mechanism (CLAUDE.md's four-flat-column description is stale). Add a small additive dashboard feature showing past escalations + message history. Placement TBD, not blocking.
- **Job-number generation — concurrency-safe fix.** Replace `MAX(job_number)+1` with an atomic mechanism (Postgres `SEQUENCE`, or a counter row via `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`). Lands with the overlay's Create mode (`generate_job_number()` currently in `projects_brief.py`).
- **`ProjectReviewer`/`ProjectApproval`** — `project_approvals` 0 rows (drop), `project_reviewers` 1 row (drop after Ezekiel eyeballs it). Not blocking.

