## Code Architecture & Data-Model Migration Plan

Verified 20 Jul 2026 against the real `app/models/__init__.py` and `app/status_tracking.py`, extended 30 Jul 2026 with the overlay-model additions.

### A. Tables to DROP
| Table | Why |
|---|---|
| `ProjectApproval` | Dead — 0 rows. |
| `ProjectReviewer` | Dead — 1 lingering row, drop after eyeball. |

### B. Columns to DROP
| Column | Why |
|---|---|
| `Deliverable.brief_flag`, `brief_flag_resolved` | Superseded by `BriefFlag`/`BriefFlagMessage`; unread/unwritten. |
| `Project.hours_accumulated`, `timer_started_at` | Hours recomputed on demand from `ProjectStatusLog`. |
| `Project.status` | `record_project_status()` only writes `project_status`. Drop, fix forward. |

### C. Fields whose MEANING changes
- **`Project.project_status`** — the live flat status. Standard: the pipeline status (In Design → Client Approved → Pre-Production → Handed to Production + On Hold/Cancelled). C&CM: `ProjectCustomer.status` is the per-customer pipeline; the C&CM project overall gets the computed aggregate (Briefed/In Progress/Design Completed).
- **`ProjectSubmission` → explicit `workflow_status` column** (additive). Backfill: `submitted_to_client_at IS NULL` → `draft`; set + `is_flagged` → `revision_requested`; set + not flagged + parent approved → `approved`; set + not flagged + parent not approved → `sent_to_client`. Old flag fields stay set alongside; removing them is a later cleanup.
- **Open decision:** clean cutover vs. backfill for in-flight projects' status the day this ships (now bigger, given the renamed/expanded vocabulary — plan the mapping carefully in the migration milestone).

### D. New tables needed
1. **`ProjectNote`** — `id, project_id, author_id, body, file_link (nullable), created_at`, + a tags mechanism (tag table or JSON array) for the future chat features.
2. **`SiteVisit`** — `id, project_id, user_id (technical), start_at, end_at, location (nullable), notes (nullable)`. Feeds the dashboard availability view + project timeline.
3. **A "has this user seen this project overlay before" marker** — `id, user_id, project_id, first_viewed_at` (drives the Project Details vs Deliverables default).
4. **`ProjectTableView`** — NOW BUILT (saved views shipped on the Projects page; see `Projects.md`). Listed here only to correct the old "not built" note.

### E. New columns / values needed
- `Project.project_owner_id` (FK users, nullable) — the Project Owner.
- **Per-deliverable pre-production layer:** `Deliverable.needs_technical`, `needs_artwork` (bool), + a technical status and an artwork status (small enums or FKs to their submission state). These are what make staggered per-deliverable pre-production free.
- `Project.is_production_only` (bool) + a pre-production requirements text field.
- **Cancelled** handling: a cancel reason (logged), reversibility. `Project.is_deleted`/`deleted_at`/`deleted_by_id` for the admin hard-delete.
- `User.role` whitelist gains `project_owner`, `finance`, `production`, `logistics`.
- Atomic job-number mechanism (SEQUENCE or `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` counter).
- `ProjectSubmission.last_internal_review_notified_at` (modified-since check), `ProjectSubmission.cs_note` (nullable).
- **Granular activity log** — either richer `log_activity` payloads (changed field, old, new) or a small structured change-log table, whichever fits cleanest. Deliverable add/remove notification wiring.

Everything else already exists: `ProjectSubmission`, `ProjectSubmissionDeliverable`, `ProjectSubmissionFile`, `TechnicalSubmission`, `ProjectRevision`/`ProjectRevisionDeliverable`, `ProjectPosmChannel`, `ProjectCustomer.installation_date`, `Project.installation_date`, `concept_options_required`/`kv_options_required`, `ProjectCustomer.posm_revision_count`, `Project.revision_count`.

### F. Gulf per-customer submission routes — logic change, not schema (see §6).

### G. Undo-Approved / file cleanup — no `previous_status` column (status logs already bracket periods); auto-copied-file cleanup can re-derive the path.

### H. Removals still ahead
Monolithic `detail.js`; the "Project Settings" floating menu; any separate Edit-Brief/Edit-Project page; dead "Remove secondary CS" modal; `flagRevision()` dead selector; `work_hours_between()`; legacy no-channel Gulf POSM path; native `confirm()` calls; old Review & Submit stale copy; the old `/projects/<id>` detail page + route (replaced by the overlay, with the `project=` param keeping inbound links alive).

